# Vulnerabilities this repository deliberately accepts. Read by the container image scans (pull
# request, release, nightly; Trivy and Grype) and by the release and nightly dependency scans of
# .github/workflows/security.yml. Pull request dependency gates do not read it: they only fail on
# what a change adds.
#
# Every entry is one ID line, directly below one comment line of this exact shape:
#   # <ID> | reason: <why it is accepted> | owner: <GitHub handle> | expires: <YYYY-MM-DD>
#   <ID>
# .github/scripts/check-trivyignore.sh fails every scan that reads this file on an entry without
# that comment, or past its expiry. Prefer fixing: an entry is for a finding that cannot be fixed
# yet, or does not apply to how the code is used, and the reason says which.
#
# Scanners can name one vulnerability differently (CVE-…, GHSA-…, GO-…): enter the ID each scanner
# reports, each with its own comment line. A dependency finding is accepted when any of its IDs or
# aliases is listed. Secrets are not accepted here: gitleaks reads .gitleaksignore and .gitleaks.toml.
#
# Example (not active):
#   # CVE-2026-0000 | reason: the vulnerable code path is in a CLI the image never runs | owner: @someone | expires: 2026-12-31
#   CVE-2026-0000
